    "answer": {
      "short": "Even.",
      "worked": "The domain is $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{-1,1\\}$, which is symmetric about $0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{(-x)^3}{(-x)^3+1}+\\frac{(-x)^3}{(-x)^3-1}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{x^3}{x^3-1}+\\frac{x^3}{x^3+1}\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence $f$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
